From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:09:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: build-locked single-process Social Club

Port the page bridge, renderer loop and IPC split from willfaust/Madeira (61dce1d, 293cd39). The app turns this on by default in both builds; a dev build's PLAYPORT_SC_SINGLE=0 turns it off (decision 0169, PLA-602). Preflight the exact opened helper before changing the process policy; a mismatch retains the multi-process policy. Carry the successful decision on the child thread and recheck before writing, failing the load closed on a changed image. A verified browser also gets --disable-component-update unless its command line has it (decision 0150 as amended 2026-10-30): its component updater asks for BITS, which starts an i386 dllhost that finds no WoW64 window under the Social Club layout. It also gets --disable-gpu and --disable-gpu-compositing, each unless present (0150 amended again 2026-10-30): decision 0109's software drawing, so the helper loads no ANGLE or Direct3D stack; --in-process-gpu adds nothing to --single-process.

The guarded build is Social Club 2.4.0.302's SocialClubHelper.exe (TimeDateStamp 0x6aeb6937, SizeOfImage 0x26e000; PLA-866), which RDR2's Steam depot installs since November 2026; 2.4.0.240's (0x6a86d563, 0x244000) is no longer accepted. Every RVA, hook site, displaced instruction and guarded window was mapped from the old build to the new one and checked instruction by instruction: the code each hook relies on is unchanged but moved, the structure offsets the thunks use (MessageLoop 0x160/0x128, IPC manager 0x1a30/0xf0/0x198+0x88, renderer app 0x60, window payload +0x188) are the same, Initialize's first instruction now stores RBX at [rsp+0x10], and the renderer's Channel Response keeps its CefString wrapper in RDI. The .text and .data zero tails moved by 0x24000 and 0x29000.

Class: host-app
Evidence: docs/decisions/0150-dev-single-process-social-club.md; tools/tests/sc_single (host checks; the 2.4.0.302 phone gate is PLA-866's)
Offered-upstream: no
